==== stdout ====
raphael help revisions - Safe writes, conflicts, archives and unknown outcomes.

A revision is a positive integer returned when an item is read. Update, move,
archive and restore check it before changing anything. Pass --revision to apply
a change only to the version you read. For changes other than body replacements,
omitting --revision makes the CLI read the current revision first and pin the
subsequent write to that same id. Body replacements require an explicit
--revision.

Exit 4 means stored state prevented the change and nothing was applied. For a
revision conflict, run get again, compare your intended change with the current
item, then retry with its new revision. Do not blindly replace the revision and
overwrite a concurrent edit. A slug conflict can also be caused by an archived
item: choose another slug or restore the existing item.

Archiving an item hides it and its descendants from ordinary lists and search.
--include-archived includes active and archived items. Archived items retain
their slugs. Restore removes only the cause archive put on the item itself; an
archived ancestor, or a cause set by something other than archive, keeps the
item archived. Read it again and restore the blocking ancestor when appropriate.

Exit 7 means a write was sent and its outcome is unknown. Read the item to
reconcile before deciding whether to try again. For an uncertain create, read
the intended path; retrying create may encounter your own slug collision. Exit 6
means retrying may work and the change was not applied.

Examples:
  raphael get /work/idea --json
  raphael update /work/idea --title 'Revised idea' --revision 3
  raphael list /work --include-archived

Next: raphael help reference
